      "text": "First, let's calculate the total number of books. Since there are 1335 boxes and each box contains 39 books, we can find the total number of books by multiplying these two numbers:\n\n\\[\n1335 \\times 39\n\\]\n\nTo perform the multiplication, we can break it down into simpler steps:\n\n\\[\n1335 \\times 39 = 1335 \\times (40 - 1) = 1335 \\times 40 - 1335 \\times 1\n\\]\n\nCalculating each part separately:\n\n\\[\n1335 \\times 40 = 53400\n\\]\n\\[\n1335 \\times 1 = 1335\n\\]\n\nSubtracting these results gives:\n\n\\[\n53400 - 1335 = 52065\n\\]\n\nSo, there are 52065 books in total.\n\nNext, we need to determine how many boxes of 40 books each can be made from these 52065 books, and how many books will be left over. We do this by dividing 52065 by 40:\n\n\\[\n52065 \\div 40\n\\]\n\nPerforming the division:\n\n\\[\n52065 \\div 40 = 1301 \\text{ R } 25\n\\]\n\nThis means that 1301 boxes can be packed with 40 books each, and there will be 25 books left over. Therefore, the number of books left over is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{25}\n\\]",
