    {
      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To determine how many books Melvin will have left over after repacking them into boxes of 40 books each, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total number of books in the warehouse.\n2. Determine how many full boxes of 40 books can be made from these books.\n3. Find out how many books are left over after packing the maximum number of full boxes.\n\n**Step 1: Calculate the total number of books.**\n\nThe warehouse contains 1335 boxes, each containing 39 books. Therefore, the total number of books is:\n\\[\n1335 \\times 39\n\\]\n\nFirst, we perform the multiplication:\n\\[\n1335 \\times 39 = 1335 \\times (40 - 1) = 1335 \\times 40 - 1335 \\times 1\n\\]\n\\[\n1335 \\times 40 = 53400\n\\]\n\\[\n1335 \\times 1 = 1335\n\\]\n\\[\n1335 \\times 39 = 53400 - 1335 = 52065\n\\]\n\nSo, the total number of books is 52065.\n\n**Step 2: Determine how many full boxes of 40 books can be made.**\n\nWe need to divide the total number of books by 40 to find out how many full boxes we can make:\n\\[\n52065 \\div 40\n\\]\n\nPerform the division:\n\\[\n52065 \\div 40 = 1301 \\text{ R } 25\n\\]\nThis means that 52065 divided by 40 gives a quotient of 1301 and a remainder of 25. The quotient 1301 represents the number of full boxes, and the remainder 25 represents the number of books left over.\n\n**Conclusion:**\n\nAfter packing as many boxes of 40 books as possible, Melvin has \\(\\boxed{25}\\) books left over.",
